From d49a193c4bf32337fa975e485f180d6ae359ed87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Hope <15705900+gabehope@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:54:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] WebGPU kernels read their sizes and constants from
 uniforms

A kernel's thread count and its nonzero numeric constants (thresholds,
offsets, lengths in index arithmetic) are read from a uniform buffer
instead of being written into the WGSL, so kernels that differ only in
those values generate the same source and share one compiled pipeline.
What stays in the source: the expression's structure and dtypes, the
tuning choices (upcast, unroll, groups), zero and boolean constants,
integer divisors (so division by a constant still compiles to shifts and
multiplies) and reduction lengths (a literal trip count lets the shader
compiler unroll the loop; measured 2x on a 512-long reduction).

- The workgroup size of ungrouped kernels is fixed at 256, and the thread
  index uses one formula for 1-D and 2-D grids.
- Nullary kernels go through the same path; nullaryKernel.ts, which did
  this for kernels without inputs, is removed.
- Sort and argsort read the array length and the workgroups per batch
  from their uniforms (as a shift), so lengths past two workgroups share
  one shader.
- Uniforms go through one shared buffer written with queue.writeBuffer()
  before each submit, instead of a new buffer per dispatch that was never
  destroyed.
- The per-kernel shader cache is bounded (least recently used, 4096).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
